Download a completed scan's report.

The body is streamed to stdout — redirect to a file with
"> report.<ext>". Format is selected with --format (json|csv|pdf,
default json).

Usage:
  usulnet recon scan report <scan-id> [flags]

Examples:
  usulnet recon scan report <scan-id> > report.json
  usulnet recon scan report <scan-id> --format csv > report.csv
  usulnet recon scan report <scan-id> --format pdf > report.pdf

Flags:
      --format string   report format: json|csv|pdf (default "json")
  -h, --help            help for report

Global Flags:
  -c, --config string   config file path (default: /etc/usulnet/config.yaml or ./config.yaml)
      --json            shortcut for --output json (overrides --output)
      --output string   output format: table|json|yaml (default "table")
  -q, --quiet           suppress informational output (errors and primary data still print)
      --server string   usulnet API URL (default $USULNET_API_URL)
      --token string    API token (default $USULNET_API_TOKEN)
